Story: Flying a VTOL with the TX15
  As a pilot with a TX15
  I want to fly the VTOL with the radio as I fly the real plane
  So that I know the radio, its screen and the plane work together before I go to the field

  This tutorial uses the radio as it is on the real plane. The TX15 sends its sticks and switches
  on a serial line, and the plane answers on the screen of the TX15. You arm the plane with SE,
  and you pick QLOITER with button 2. Push the throttle stick up, and the plane climbs straight
  up. Press button 3 for FBWA, and the plane flies forward on its wing and levels itself. Bank it
  with the aileron stick, and let go. Press button 2 to hover again, and press button 6. The plane
  flies home and lands softly. At each step, look at the screen of the TX15.

  Scenario: Arm, lift off, fly forward in FBWA, hover again and land softly
    When the arm switch is on
    Then the vehicle is armed
    And the TX15 screen arming is armed
    When the mode switch is QLOITER
    Then the autopilot mode is QLOITER
    And the TX15 screen mode is QLOITER
    When the throttle stick is high
    Then the flight is hovering
    And the plane is flying
    And the height above home is at least 15 m
    When the pilot switches to forward flight
    Then the flight is cruising
    And the autopilot mode is FBWA
    And the TX15 screen mode is FBWA
    When the aileron stick is right
    Then the VTOL's wings are banked
    When the aileron stick is centred
    Then the VTOL's wings are level
    When the pilot switches back to a hover
    Then the flight is hovering
    And the autopilot mode is QLOITER
    And the TX15 screen mode is QLOITER
    When the pilot sends the plane home
    Then the autopilot mode is QRTL
    And the plane is on the ground
    And the last landing is soft
    And the TX15 screen arming is disarmed
